#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064169 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064040 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/id #uuid "c25e6037-3900-5314-b9a9-262fef07061c" :question/math-academy-id "e-368" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac 1 {x^3}$ and that $F'(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if\n\n$$\nF'(x) = f(x)\n$$\n\nthen integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF^{′}(x) &= f(x) \\\\\n\\intF^{′}(x)dx &= \\intf(x)dx \\\\\nF(x) &= \\intf(x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 {x^3}= x^{-3}\n$$\n\nSo, we can use the power rule with $n=-3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(x) &= \\intf(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&= \\intx^{-3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{-3 + 1}}{-3 + 1} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{x^{-2}}{2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502964 :question-generator/id #uuid "b6ea070b-44e4-510d-a59c-ee47a984c30f" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186064169.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064722 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a907ad-e7e6-5e6b-abb5-c41f16606605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062390} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6a8d1e-0787-5cc4-88df-ddf958e1c1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x^{-1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062391} {:answer/id #uuid "16cba4e2-5699-54d0-b0af-01f1431acd0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x^{5/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062392} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2e4389-0b1c-5925-9f9f-a24ca4b82e65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062393} {:answer/id #uuid "70c4a8d8-2ed6-56b1-a746-7e1fc22b8346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x^{-1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062394}] :answer-field/id #uuid "29757ce8-69c0-518a-9094-1478bb25152b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062389}] :question/id #uuid "35560944-ec26-532a-8ab4-c27135900127" :question/math-academy-id "q-29987" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = x^{-2/3}$ and that $F^{′}(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064723 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af3857a5-22ad-5617-8dd5-fe36c075509e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}x^{3/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062396} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2aaad4-968f-574b-842f-23871805d75b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062397} {:answer/id #uuid "35a1e4d4-ceef-5bb3-8381-e67a3cd0b1b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}x^{5/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062398} {:answer/id #uuid "40c5bb75-6c13-5d38-b5c4-d450f209706c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062399} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb175d1-16eb-5478-ba97-5cb4d5899d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062400}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4af9582e-4d65-5832-94c1-0ccba896c739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062395}] :question/id #uuid "4f854a01-0859-5bcc-add9-c9a801f5da45" :question/math-academy-id "q-29989" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x^{3/5}}$ and that $F^{′}(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25edeff2-faa4-50c4-bbfd-3291d7ac7694" :question/math-academy-id "q-113705" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4/3}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4/3}}={x}^{-4/3}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/3}}{(-\\frac{1}{3})}+C \\\\  & =-3{x}^{-1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{1/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233751 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a192223-274d-5d58-847a-c92d2faa98df" :question/math-academy-id "q-29633" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}={x}^{-4}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-4$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{-4+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dcd24a2-ce5f-5ab6-8a92-814e8f1355a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-29662" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/2}}={x}^{-5/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}} & =\\int {x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/2+1}}{-\\frac{5}{2}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3{x}^{3/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44529618-fcf7-5581-8bd3-a0df68de242f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71100" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/7}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/7+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{7}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6/7}}{(\\frac{6}{7})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{6/7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "379ce176-b85b-5473-ac5c-c334e33ade53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502889} {:answer/id #uuid "3fa0d404-d0fc-5e09-8e4b-7fcc8eed12b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-13/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502896} {:answer/id #uuid "4028963f-e622-507c-92ba-3fe653d44e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{7}x^{-20/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502898} {:answer/id #uuid "48e20e30-98ef-545f-8564-315ec67ca5ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502906} {:answer/id #uuid "d873e68a-b191-51b0-8a82-9ae3df09c4fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{7}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48e20e30-98ef-545f-8564-315ec67ca5ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{6}x^{-6/7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502906} :answer-field/id #uuid "94d70d54-a73e-59c2-9e26-72bd20515cfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "054c92af-f6c0-5cb6-8c52-c81bf5740a21" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{13/7}}={x}^{-13/7}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{13}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[7]{{x}^{13}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-13/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-13/7+1}}{-\\frac{13}{7}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{-6/7}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{6{x}^{6/7}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502872 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e03f87-24cd-5a1f-85f6-21fa74293d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{9}x^{-16/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502861} {:answer/id #uuid "04c21815-61ed-534e-ad04-3d35a62aa2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502862} {:answer/id #uuid "24baf7d8-b08d-52e8-aacf-0f682f6c25f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{9}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502877} {:answer/id #uuid "a8a05915-00e3-5287-9df3-ec5051320330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{-7/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502937} {:answer/id #uuid "d1cf8368-4008-5f0c-b393-98dc8c2b3340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04c21815-61ed-534e-ad04-3d35a62aa2bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{2}x^{2/9} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502862} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d96cda-06e3-5949-b59a-136c6439133a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 