 "80af63e6-f7fb-5178-9c4a-d96bedf2c287" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x^{-5/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502922} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d97a02-3bcb-5f85-9497-a9db944bdb62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502942} {:answer/id #uuid "e0d65c81-82ee-5c39-9813-d7adc6117dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502955} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b9e661-3c29-5b89-b031-ae16b8d1203b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502957}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b9e661-3c29-5b89-b031-ae16b8d1203b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}x^{3/4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502957} :answer-field/id #uuid "10312bb4-8cd0-5e43-95e8-b8afad9283e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a5e9787-8ef9-5e19-99e9-70e48a27adcf" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/4}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/4+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/4}}{(\\frac{3}{4})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3/4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502900 :knowledge-point/_questions [{