nswer/value "\\frac{5}{4}x^{4/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502916} :answer-field/id #uuid "0019a5a4-b1cd-503a-b7ea-8aa8c7427461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7466173d-cde9-509d-97b9-e88aaf8822fd" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/5}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/5+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/5}}{(\\frac{4}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{x}^{4/5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d4daf1-ba4b-5a5a-9bfb-9fcfa0ec5e3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-8/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502867} {:answer/id #uuid "16537613-9cc7-5cb0-93b0-7503cdac3395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-3/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502868} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2dd136-0894-52fa-aaf0-fb2dc0ac21a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}x^{-13/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502894} {:answer/id #uuid "718ee9a6-017b-59f0-8c6e-948645ffc5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :an